      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ كَسَرَ يَدَ رَجُلٍ ثُمَّ بَرَأَتْ يَدُ اَلرَّجُلِ فَقَالَ\n\"لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ فِي هَذَا قِصَاصٌ وَ لَكِنَّهُ يُعْطِي اَلْأَرْشَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5393 - Jameel ibn Darraj narrated from some of our companions from one of the two Imams (as) regarding a man who broke another man's hand, and then the man's hand healed.\nImam (as) said: \"There is no retaliation (qisas) in this case, but he must pay compensation (Al-arsh).\""
        ]
      }
